  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Awareness Raising For Labour Mobility to Bulgaria</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The labour migration flow from Armenia, Moldova and Georgia is expected to increase based on bilateral agreements signed between Bulgaria and the three countries in 2018 and 2019.Trying to regulate better rights of foreign workers, Bulgaria has concluded bilateral labour migration agreements with Armenia, Georgia and Moldova. Against this background, the project seeks to assess the information needs of citizens of Armenia, Georgia and Moldova and increase their awareness on legal aspects, rights and responsibilities of citizens from these countries in Bulgaria, legal aspects related to employment in Bulgaria such as a need for a work permit, recognition of qualifications and other information related to Bulgarian labour market, unemployment rate, salary levels for different sectors, access to social and health benefits, taxes and social payments, risks and prevention of labour exploitation, access to migrant workers&#xB4; support organisations, etc.</narrative>
  </description>
